# Home Assistant glossary

This page covers every entry in the [official Home Assistant glossary](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/glossary/) snapshot checked on 12 November 2026. The native terms and aliases remain recognisable. The explanations below are original civica wording for household tasks, not a replacement translation or a copy of the official definitions.

Read [how to use the terminology register](home-assistant-terminology.html) before treating an explanation as an interface label. For literal state values, device classes and platform identifiers, use [Entity and state language](entity-and-state-language.html).

## Distinctions that matter during a task

An integration supplies entities; a device can group several of them. A trigger starts a run, a condition checks whether it can continue, and an action requests an operation. Saving or enabling an automation does not establish that the action ran. A notification being sent does not establish that someone read it.

