## Browse the glossary

<% register = JSON.parse(File.read(File.join(root, 'data', 'ha-terminology.json'))) %>
<% sources = register['sources'].to_h { |source| [source['id'], source] } %>
<% entries = register['terms'].select { |term| term['category'] == 'official-glossary' }.sort_by { |term| term['native_name'].downcase } %>
<% letters = entries.map { |term| term['native_name'][0].upcase }.uniq %>
<nav aria-label="Glossary letters"><p><% letters.each_with_index do |letter, index| %><%= ' · ' unless index.zero? %><a href="#letter-<%= letter.downcase %>"><%= letter %></a><% end %></p></nav>

<% letters.each do |letter| %>
<h2 id="letter-<%= letter.downcase %>"><%= letter %></h2>
<% entries.select { |term| term['native_name'][0].upcase == letter }.each do |term| %>
<details class="civica-audit-detail" id="<%= escape(term['id'].downcase) %>">
<summary><strong><%= escape(term['native_name']) %></strong><%= ' — historical term retained' if term['status'] == 'historical-term-retained' %></summary>
<p><strong>Household wording:</strong> <%= escape(term['household_wording']) %>.</p>
<p><strong>First-use explanation:</strong> <%= escape(term['first_use_explanation']) %></p>
<p><strong>Keep distinct:</strong> <%= escape(term['avoid_confusion']) %></p>
<% unless term['aliases'].empty? %><p><strong>Aliases recorded by the source:</strong> <%= escape(term['aliases'].join(', ')) %>. These are lookup references, not instructions to replace native labels.</p><% end %>
<p><a href="<%= escape(term['official_glossary_url']) %>">Official <%= escape(term['native_name']) %> entry</a><% if term['further_reading_url'] %> · <a href="<%= escape(term['further_reading_url']) %>">Related official guidance</a><% end %>. Reference: <code><%= escape(term['id']) %></code>.</p>
</details>
<% end %>
<% end %>

## Historical terms and current instructions

Apps were formerly called add-ons. Lovelace remains in technical dashboard identifiers. Component was an older name for integration, while “component” also has a separate meaning in this design system. Home Assistant Core remains the main program even though the former standalone Core production installation method is deprecated. Home Assistant Supervised names a deprecated installation method; Supervisor is still a distinct software component.

Preserve those distinctions. Use the current control name when giving a current instruction, and retain an old literal key when explaining saved configuration. Link to the [current official installation guidance](https://www.home-assistant.io/installation/) before recommending an installation method.

## Scope and maintenance

The register maps 83 source entries, not every phrase in the entire Home Assistant website. Source snapshots, aliases, entry identifiers and reviewed dates are in the [terminology JSON](../reference/ha-terminology.json). The [interface terminology chapter](interface-terminology.html) adds the specifically enumerated native UI and configuration vocabulary. Future or vendor-specific terms need a separate source check.
